# UI Consistency

When editing `.tsx` or `.css` files in this project:

1. Consult `.cursor/skills/ui-consistency/STANDARDS.md` before making UI changes.
2. Prefer `components/ui/*` and `lib/ui-tokens.ts` over duplicated inline Tailwind classes.
3. Category colors must come from `lib/col-config.ts` (`COL_CONFIG`).
4. Functional colors (deadline, reply, buttons) use `functionalColors` from `lib/ui-tokens.ts`.
5. **Never use dynamic Tailwind classes** in `className` template literals (e.g. `` `hover:${x}` ``).
6. **Icons must use Tabler** via `components/ui/Icon` — no inline SVG, emoji icons, or direct `@tabler/icons-react` imports.
7. **Do not change visual appearance** — refactors must preserve the same final Tailwind classes on the DOM.
8. **Propose changes and wait for user confirmation** before editing (see `ui-consistency` skill).
9. Do not suggest visual improvements, redesigns, dark mode, or responsive overhauls.
10. After significant UI changes, run:
   ```bash
   node .cursor/skills/ui-consistency/scripts/validate-ui.mjs
   ```

## Shared primitives

Use these instead of copying class strings:

- `DotIndicator`, `Pill`, `AiChip`, `Card`, `Button`, `EmptyState`, `ColumnHeader`, `Icon`, `TileIcon`

## Allowed custom font sizes

`text-[9px]`, `text-[10px]`, `text-[11px]`, `text-[12px]`, `text-[13px]`, plus `text-lg`, `text-xl`, `text-sm`, `text-xs`.
